export const FOUNDER_SCIENCE_COPY = {
  "AVK-FS-FI-01": "Founder",
  "AVK-FS-FI-02": "From Questions to Worlds",
  "AVK-FS-FI-03": "AvatarK began with a question that traces back to BITS Pilani, where Devendar Pallapati arrived to study engineering in 1986: What builds the engineer before the engineer builds the world?",
  "AVK-FS-FI-04": "The four chapters of the Founder Letter follow that question through three decades of building technology, a return to Indian philosophical traditions, the architecture for becoming that grew from them, and the Living Worlds through which AvatarK hopes to give what a life has learned a place to continue.",
  "AVK-FS-FI-05": "The letter is a personal account, written in the first person. Where it describes what AvatarK is building, it distinguishes what exists today from what is still being designed.",
  "AVK-FS-FT-01": "Along the way",
  "AVK-FS-FT-10": "1986",
  "AVK-FS-FT-11": "Arrives at BITS Pilani to study engineering and works on the student magazine Setpoint.",
  "AVK-FS-FT-20": "After BITS Pilani",
  "AVK-FS-FT-21": "Completes a master's degree in computer science in the United States.",
  "AVK-FS-FT-30": "Three decades",
  "AVK-FS-FT-31": "Works across enterprise software, distributed systems, semiconductors and artificial intelligence, including part of a career at IBM.",
  "AVK-FS-FT-40": "Later",
  "AVK-FS-FT-41": "Returns to Indian philosophical traditions; with Prometheus as the fourth axis, the Four Axes of the Canon take shape.",
  "AVK-FS-FT-50": "Today",
  "AVK-FS-FT-51": "Founder of AvatarK. Living Forest, the first Persistent Living World, is in development through WorldK.",
  "AVK-FS-FC-01": "Echo and Living Worlds",
  "AVK-FS-FC-02": "Echo is designed to keep what a life has learned. Living Worlds are designed to give that learning a place, where others can arrive, notice what has changed and return. One carries a life forward through memory; the other, through place.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-01": "Method",
  "AVK-FS-FM-02": "How AvatarK Investigates and Builds",
  "AVK-FS-FM-03": "AvatarK draws on philosophy, story, science and engineering. Each does different work, and we try not to let one stand in for another. Four working commitments keep them distinct.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-10": "Inquiry",
  "AVK-FS-FM-11": "We begin with questions about how people attend, decide, take responsibility and contribute. Philosophical traditions and stories are one source of those questions. They inspire the work; they are not offered as evidence for it.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-20": "Evidence",
  "AVK-FS-FM-21": "Before we rely on an idea, we look at what is already known about it, and we state what we expect to happen as a hypothesis: a claim that could turn out to be wrong.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-30": "Engineering",
  "AVK-FS-FM-31": "We build systems that can be inspected, measured and changed: designed against stated requirements, tested before release and corrected when they fall short.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-40": "Evaluation",
  "AVK-FS-FM-41": "We say that a practice or product helps only when it has been evaluated, and we describe how. Where something has not yet been evaluated, we say so.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-50": "Four kinds of statement",
  "AVK-FS-FM-51": "Inspiration — a philosophical idea or story that suggests a question. The Four Axes of the Canon belong here.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-52": "Hypothesis — a claim we expect to be true and intend to test.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-53": "Implementation — something that has been built and can be used, observed or inspected.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-54": "Validated outcome — a result that has been evaluated, with the method described.",
  "AVK-FS-FM-55": "Most of what AvatarK describes today is inspiration, hypothesis or early implementation. We will not present any of it as a validated outcome until it has been evaluated.",
  "AVK-FS-CI-01": "A contemporary reading",
  "AVK-FS-CI-02": "Each axis can also be read as a question that any person, team or institution might ask. These readings are AvatarK's interpretation. They do not change what the axes mean in the Canon, and they are not scientific claims.",
  "AVK-FS-CI-11": "Am I paying attention to what is actually happening, around me and within me, before I act?",
  "AVK-FS-CI-21": "Can I make a sound judgment when the situation is complex, values conflict and the outcome is uncertain?",
  "AVK-FS-CI-31": "Will I act on what I know, keep my commitments and accept the consequences of my choices?",
  "AVK-FS-CI-41": "What will I make or give that is useful to someone other than myself?",
  "AVK-FS-CI-50-R": "Adiyogi, Krishna and Rama appear in the Canon as inspirations drawn from Indian philosophical, religious and epic traditions; Prometheus, from Greek myth and literary traditions. AvatarK does not present them as historical or scientific authorities, and does not derive scientific conclusions from them.",
  "AVK-FS-CI-51": "How AvatarK investigates and builds →"
} as const

